counterfactuals.output:
A respiratory interface for delivery of pressurized breathable gas to a user, comprising:

a mask body defining a breathing chamber and configured to be positioned adjacent a nasal region of the user without overlying a bridge of the user’s nose;

a sealing arrangement coupled to the mask body, the sealing arrangement comprising first and second laterally spaced sealing portions configured to engage and seal against opposing side surfaces of the nasal region, while leaving the nose bridge substantially uncovered;

one or more reinforcing support members associated with the mask body and/or the sealing arrangement, the reinforcing support members being configured to limit, direct, or otherwise control expansion, deformation, or outward displacement of the mask body or sealing arrangement under application of positive airway pressure;

one or more cover members disposed over at least a portion of the reinforcing support members and/or the sealing arrangement, the cover members being configured to distribute forces, maintain seal geometry, and enhance user comfort; and

wherein the sealing arrangement is provided in a plurality of selectable configurations, sizes, or geometries corresponding to different nasal dimensions, including at least one of nose width, nostril spacing, nasal sidewall contour, or nasal height, such that a selected sealing arrangement provides sealing engagement with the opposing sides of the nasal region without requiring contact with the nose bridge.

In some embodiments, the respiratory interface is a continuous positive airway pressure (CPAP) mask configured to receive pressurized gas from a CPAP device through an inlet coupled to the mask body.

In some embodiments, the reinforcing support members comprise ribs, frames, inserts, stays, or semi-rigid structures embedded in, attached to, or positioned adjacent the sealing arrangement.

In some embodiments, the cover members comprise flexible, resilient, or fabric-like layers configured to enclose or overlay the reinforcing support members to reduce localized pressure on the user.

In some embodiments, the plurality of selectable seal configurations includes different lateral spacings, seal thicknesses, seal curvatures, or contact-surface profiles adapted to accommodate varying user nose shapes while maintaining clearance from the nasal bridge.
